$( STATEMENT OF CONJECTURE:
   For any positive whole number n (except -13), if you repeatedly multiply 
   the number by 2, add 13, and take the base-10 digit sum of the result, 
   the sequence will always stabilize into one of the following finite 
   attractor loops: {3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11}.
$) the more specific loops are 
 the loop where it is a never ending 5 
the loop where it bounces between 8 and 11 
and the loop where 3 ,  4 , 6 , 7 , 9 , and 10 may come in any order 


